---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";

const updated = "26 August 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Cluetune handles data: no accounts, stats stay in your browser, and we do not sell personal information."
>
  <article class="page-shell py-8 sm:py-16">
    <header class="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-body-sm text-mute">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-12 flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-8 text-body-md text-body">
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          Cluetune ({SITE.domain}) is a free guess-the-song game. You do not create an account. We
          do not run a player database. If you never email us, we never receive your name.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Streaks, stats, theme preference and the daily result are stored in this browser’s
          localStorage under keys prefixed <span class="font-mono text-body-sm">cluetune:</span>.
          That data does not leave your device unless you export it from the{" "}
          <a href="/stats" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">Stats</a> page. Clearing
          site data or switching phones deletes it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">What the server sees</h2>
        <p>
          When you play, your browser requests a round and search suggestions. Those requests include
          a typical IP address, user-agent and the query you typed in the guess box. We use that to
          return a playable clip and autocomplete — not to build a profile. Hosting (for example
          Vercel) and CDN logs may retain request metadata for a short period under their own terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Third-party audio, lyrics and charts</h2>
        <p>
          Preview clips stream directly from Apple Music and Deezer. Lyric snippets for Lyrics Guess
          come from LRCLIB. Chart metadata may come from those services and, when configured,
          Spotify. Their privacy policies apply to those requests. Cluetune does not host, cache or
          re-serve audio files.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to understand how people find and use the site (page views,
          referrers, device type). Google may set cookies such as <span class="font-mono text-body-sm">_ga</span> for
          that purpose. We do not use it for advertising and we do not sell that data. A theme
          preference is stored locally, not as a tracking cookie.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions:{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">{SITE.email}</a>
          {" "}or the{" "}
          <a href="/contact" class="text-link underline underline-offset-4">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
